{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>He has not beheld iniquity in Jacob</b> This refers back to the El who was mentioned (Numbers 23:19). He says that HaShem has not beheld iniquity and falsehood in Jacob, nor seen in them trouble and anger that they commit before Him, and therefore He is with them and the shout of His kingship is among them, for He will shout, He will raise the battle cry against their enemies whenever He prevails. This is the opinion of R. Abraham Ibn Ezra, and it is correct. It is also possible to interpret further that \"אָוֶן\" in this place is like \"Under אָוֶן I saw the tents of Cushan\" (Habakkuk 3:7), and עָמָל is like it, and likewise \"Under his tongue is עָמָל וָאָוֶן\" (Psalms 10:7) — falsehood and lies, for a thing that will not be and will not come about, because it is false, is called אָוֶן and עָמָל, since nothing reaches a person from it except toil. He says: Behold, to bless I have taken, and He has blessed, and I will not reverse it, for no man has beheld אָוֶן in Jacob, nor has any person seen falsehood in Israel — their trust is not a lie and their hope is not false, but all their blessings and their trust will endure forever, in the language of \"Behold, such is our מַבָּט\" (Isaiah 20:6), \"And they shall be dismayed and ashamed of Cush, their מַבָּט\" (ibid. verse 5), and likewise \"And you have not looked to the Maker thereof, nor considered Him who fashioned it long ago\" (ibid. 22:11) — the matter of trust and hope. And he gave the reason: for YHWH their Elohim is with Him, who does not lie and does not relent, and the shout of a mighty King is among them, who will never be defeated, for when He brought them out of Egypt, behold, to Him was great strength like the horns of the wild ox above every beast, and how could all their blessings not be fulfilled, with no divination and omen among them:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:08:19.000619474Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}